\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

Coupling alignment---optimizing through the output distribution---is the dominant design dimension for learned sparsity: signal type accounts for 97.5\% of the PPL gap, while cross-layer coupling contributes downstream fidelity (3--4\,pp on ARC-c, WinoGrande).
A predictor ($<$1\% of base) reduces TEAL's perplexity by 14.5\%, with KL-discovered masks (46--68\% divergent from magnitude) driving inference quality; however, downstream transfer is task- and scale-dependent.
Future work includes N:M structured sparsity and scaling to 70B+.
